#---
# purpose: "a panic whose value is not an exception rescues as an ErlangError carrying the value as original, by alias and by bare variable"
# oracle: 00819_a_panic_with_a_plain_value_rescues_as_an_erlang_error.oracle.exs
#---
# Elixir normalizes a few reason atoms into named exceptions (`:badarg`
# becomes ArgumentError); fz does not, so the value here is one Elixir leaves
# alone. The oracle spells the panic as `:erlang.error/1`.
def main() do
  by_alias = try do
    panic(:boom)
  rescue
    e in ErlangError -> e.original
  end
  dbg(by_alias)
  bare = try do
    panic({:stop, 3})
  rescue
    e -> {e.__struct__, e.original}
  end
  dbg(bare)
end
